yoyo index <path> now indexes only the files under that path, and bare yoyo grep now exits 2. It's committed as 10a34b86 with Part of #982, and build, test, clippy and fmt all pass.

What I measured first (the built binary, run from a temp dir with README.md, top.rs and sub/a.rs):
• `index /nonexistent, index sub and plain index` all printed the same three-file table of the current directory and exited 0. The path argument was being thrown away.
• Bare grep printed its usage text and exited 0, while bare def and outline exit 2.

What it does now:

| command | before | after |
|---|---|---|
| index /nonexistent | whole cwd table, exit 0 | ✗ no such path: … on stderr, exit 1 |
| index sub | whole cwd table | only sub/a.rs, exit 0 |
| index a b / index --all | whole cwd table | error on stderr, nothing on stdout, exit 2 |
| bare index | exit 0 | unchanged |
| index <existing empty dir> | — | "(no indexable source files found)", exit 0 |
| bare grep | usage, exit 0 | same usage text, exit 2 |
| grep <no match> | exit 0 | unchanged |

Why I honoured the path rather than refusing it: the index builder now takes the file list and an optional path filter, so it could use the path without touching a fourth file. The filter works the same way as /map [path] (a prefix match on project paths, with ./ stripped). A missing path goes through /map's existing check and exit code (1), so there is no second classifier. The arguments are passed through unchanged, so a path containing a space stays one path.

One extra change: grep -s with no pattern also exits 2 now, because the parser treats it the same as bare grep.

Tests: three new tests in tests/integration.rs run the built binary and compare the full stdout for every case above, including the three that should still exit 0. For the positive control, I broke the grep exit, the path filter and the missing-path exit in one mutate→test→restore command. The index and grep tests failed by name, and the bare-index test stayed green, which is what should happen. The restore is clean.

Other files changed:
• **Size limits:** `tests/module_size.rs` raises the recorded sizes of `commands_search.rs` (4460 → 4573; 44 of those lines were already over the limit before this task) and dispatch_sub.rs (2203 → 2213).
• Docs: docs/src/usage/commands.md now lists yoyo index [path] and the new exit codes.
• **Measurement:** a new ARCHITECTURE.md entry records the measurement and what's left.
• **Issue #982:** the body is updated in place. Bare `grep` was never on the "known still exit 0" list, so that list got shorter by exactly one entry (`index`). The issue body says so.

Still not fixed:
• **Rest of #982:** bare run, config <unknown>, and the mismatch where tree/undo usage errors exit 1 but def/outline/grep/map/index exit 2.
• **REPL /index:** /index src in the REPL still never reaches this code, because the REPL only recognizes /index typed exactly.
• **Path quirks shared with /map:** an existing path outside the project quietly reports "nothing found" and exits 0. Inside a git repo, paths are matched from the repo root, so a path typed from a subdirectory doesn't match.
• **Not measured:** plain `yoyo index` run from inside a git subdirectory looks wrong (the file list is relative to the repo root but files are read relative to where you are). That was already true before this change, and I didn't test it.
